rname": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Samajh bhi nahi aaya ki kya bola", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:50:27Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "4. X spent much of his career in St. Petersburg under the patronage of Y. One legend tells of a visiting French philosopher, Denis Diderot, who was an atheist and was annoying the Russian court with his arguments.\nThe story goes that X approached Diderot and gravely informed him he had a mathematical proof of God's existence:\n\"Sir, {a + b^n}/{n} = x, therefore God exists; reply!\"\nDiderot, who allegedly knew nothing of algebra, was so embarrassed by the \"proof\" that he fled the country.\nIn 1735, X was tasked by the Paris Academy to solve a problem that had stumped the era’s greatest minds. He solved it in just three days, but the intense physical strain—combined with a high fever—cost him the sight in his right eye by 1740 and the other by 1766.\nRather than despairing, X famously remarked:\n\"Now I will have fewer distractions.”\nId X and Y.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:50:42Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "euler", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:50:45Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Euler", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:50:46Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "catherine the gerat", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:51:48Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Euler and Catherine (II) the great are correct.\nEuler and Catherine II 's mother Catherine I were born in 1707 and 1684 respectfully", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:51:58Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats